Review written to `docs/reviews/equipment-loads/equip-loads-02-scheduled-load-zip-zone-routing.md`.

**6 findings** (0 critical, 2 high, 2 medium, 2 low):

- **High**: All 20+ scheduled load types default to unity power factor with no voltage sensitivity (constant-P ZIP) — OCHRE provides per-type defaults like Lighting (Z=0.54, I=0.5, P=-0.04) and Refrigerator (Z=5.03, I=-8.48, P=4.45, pf=0.8)
- **High**: EventBasedLoad/WetAppliance have no ZIP model at all — reactive power hard-coded to 0.0
- **Medium**: "Basement MELs" load type from OCHRE not registered
- **Medium**: Exterior/outdoor name routing overrides explicit zone_id (priority inverted vs OCHRE)
- **Low**: Reactive ZIP validation error messages could be more helpful
- **Low**: Gas schedule unit switching (therms vs watts) is under-documented
